open scoped Classical
open IsDedekindDomain.HeightOneSpectrum

namespace NK.TameStructure

universe u

noncomputable section

variable {K : Type*} [Field K] [NumberField K]
    (𝔭 : IsDedekindDomain.HeightOneSpectrum (NumberField.RingOfIntegers K))

/-! ## The named classical inputs, for `κ = K_𝔭` -/

/-- **`Gal(κ(μ_{p'})/κ) ≅ Ẑ`** (NSW, *Cohomology of Number Fields*, (7.5.6) and (7.5.7)
Corollary; Serre, *Local Fields*, Ch. V §4).

For a `p`-adic field `κ = K_𝔭`, the extension obtained by adjoining all roots of unity of order
prime to `p` is the *maximal unramified extension* `κ^ur` of `κ`: the residue field of `κ` is
finite of order `q`, so `κ(μ_n)/κ` is unramified of degree `ord_n(q)` for every `n` prime to `p`,
and every unramified extension arises this way.  Consequently

  `Gal(κ(μ_{p'})/κ) ≅ Gal(𝔽̄_q/𝔽_q) ≅ Ẑ`,

topologically generated by the Frobenius (the `q`-th power map on the residue field).

This is the classical input from which the field `unramifiedQuotient` of
`NK.TameData.TameInertiaInput` is derived, through the Galois-correspondence bridge
`NK.TameStructure.TameStructure.quotient_inertiaSubgroup_mulEquiv_unramifiedClosure`. -/
def UnramifiedZhat (p : ℕ) (K : Type*) [Field K] [NumberField K]
    (𝔭 : IsDedekindDomain.HeightOneSpectrum (NumberField.RingOfIntegers K))
    (K' : Type*) [Field K'] [Algebra (𝔭.adicCompletion K) K']
    [IsSepClosure (𝔭.adicCompletion K) K'] : Prop :=
  Nonempty (Gal(↥(NK.LocalAnabelian.unramifiedClosure (κ := 𝔭.adicCompletion K) (K' := K') p) /
      𝔭.adicCompletion K) ≃* NK.LocalAnabelian.Zhat)

/-- **The structure of the tame inertia** (NSW (7.5.7) Corollary and (7.5.11); Iwasawa, *On Galois
groups of local fields*; Serre, *Local Fields* IV §2).

For `κ = K_𝔭` a `p`-adic field with separable closure `K'`, writing `V_κ` for the join of the
normal pro-`p` subgroups of `G_κ = Gal(K'/κ)` and `I_κ ⊇ V_κ` for the inertia subgroup:

* `I_κ/V_κ` is the *maximal closed normal pro-cyclic* subgroup of `G_κ/V_κ`
  (equivalently: the maximal tamely ramified extension `κ^{tr}` of `κ` is
  `κ^ur(π^{1/n} : (n,p) = 1)` for a uniformiser `π`, so that `Gal(κ^{tr}/κ^ur) ≅ ∏_{ℓ ≠ p} ℤ_ℓ`),
* `V_κ` is *closed* in `G_κ` — the classical statement that the wild inertia is a Galois group
  (Hilbert's theorem: the wild inertia of a finite Galois extension of local fields is a `p`-group,
  so `κ̄/κ^{tr}` is pro-`p`, and `V_κ = Gal(K'/κ^{tr})`).  The *definition*
  `NK.LocalTame.wildInertiaSubgroup` used in this workspace is the abstract join of the normal
  pro-`p` subgroups, which is *a priori* bigger than the closed subgroup they generate; the
  identification of the two is this field.  It is what makes the derivation of the commutator
  relation `[I_κ, I_κ] ≤ V_κ` from the pro-cyclicity of `I_κ/V_κ` possible
  (`NK.TameStructure.TameInertiaInput_commutator_mem`).

The first component contains `V_κ ≤ I_κ` (the wild inertia lies in the inertia subgroup), which is
the field `wildInertia_le_inertia` of `NK.LocalTame.TameStructureInput`.

The component `I_κ/V_κ` **pro-prime-to-`p`** of the classical statement (NSW (7.5.11)) is *not* an
input here: it is *derived* from the maximality of `V_κ` and the closedness of `V_κ` in
`NK.TameStructure.ProfiniteAux.isProPrimeToP_of_maxNormalProP` via
`NK.TameStructure.isProPrimeToP_tameInertia`. -/
def TameInertiaStructure (p : ℕ) (K : Type*) [Field K] [NumberField K]
    (𝔭 : IsDedekindDomain.HeightOneSpectrum (NumberField.RingOfIntegers K))
    (K' : Type*) [Field K'] [Algebra (𝔭.adicCompletion K) K']
    [IsSepClosure (𝔭.adicCompletion K) K'] : Prop :=
  NK.LocalTame.IsMaxNormalProCyclicInQuotient
      (NK.LocalTame.wildInertiaSubgroup (κ := 𝔭.adicCompletion K) (K' := K') p)
      (NK.LocalAnabelian.inertiaSubgroup (κ := 𝔭.adicCompletion K) (K' := K') p) ∧
    IsClosed (NK.LocalTame.wildInertiaSubgroup (κ := 𝔭.adicCompletion K) (K' := K') p :
      Set (Gal(K'/𝔭.adicCompletion K)))

/-- **The normalised Frobenius exists** (NSW (7.5.6)).

For `κ = K_𝔭` with residue field of `q` elements there is an element of `G_κ = Gal(K'/κ)` which
lies outside the inertia subgroup and acts on the roots of unity of order prime to `p` by the
`q`-th power map: the Frobenius of the unramified extension `κ(μ_{p'})/κ` acts on its residue
field `𝔽̄_q` by `x ↦ x^q`, and on the prime-to-`p` roots of unity (which are unramified, being
`(q^n - 1)`-th roots of unity of the residue field, lifted by Hensel) by `ζ ↦ ζ^q`.

Note that `IsFrobeniusFor p q x` *implies* that the roots of unity of `κ` of order prime to `p`
have order dividing `q - 1` (they are fixed by `x`), i.e. this input carries the classical
statement `μ_{q-1} ⊆ κ` together with the Frobenius normalisation `ζ ↦ ζ^q`.

This is exactly the classical content of the structure `NK.LocalAnabelian.ResidueCardInput`, in
the `𝔭`-adic setting. -/
def ResidueFrobenius (p q : ℕ) (K : Type*) [Field K] [NumberField K]
    (𝔭 : IsDedekindDomain.HeightOneSpectrum (NumberField.RingOfIntegers K))
    (K' : Type*) [Field K'] [Algebra (𝔭.adicCompletion K) K']
    [IsSepClosure (𝔭.adicCompletion K) K'] : Prop :=
  ∃ x : Gal(K'/𝔭.adicCompletion K),
    NK.LocalAnabelian.IsFrobeniusFor (κ := 𝔭.adicCompletion K) (K' := K') p q x

/-- **The Frobenius normalisation** (NSW (12.1.8) Lemma; Iwasawa).

For `κ = K_𝔭` with residue field of `q` elements, the Frobenius element is *normalised by its
action on the tame inertia*:

* some element acting on the prime-to-`p` roots of unity by `ζ ↦ ζ^q` (the normalised Frobenius,
  whose existence is `NK.TameStructure.ResidueFrobenius`) conjugates the tame inertia `I_κ/V_κ`
  by the `q`-th power map;
* conversely, an element conjugating `I_κ/V_κ` by the `q`-th power map acts on the prime-to-`p`
  roots of unity by `ζ ↦ ζ^q` — the injectivity of the cyclotomic character
  `G_κ/I_κ ↪ Aut(I_κ/V_κ) = ∏_{ℓ ≠ p} ℤ_ℓ^×`.

These are the two fields of `NK.LocalStructure.TameFrobeniusCore`, so that
`NK.TameStructure.tameFrobeniusCore_adicCompletion` is a direct repackaging; the mathematical
content is the identification, via Kummer theory for the tame extension `κ^{tr} = κ^ur(π^{1/n})`,
of the `G_κ`-module `I_κ/V_κ` with the Tate twist `∏_{ℓ ≠ p} ℤ_ℓ(1)`. -/
def FrobeniusNormalisation (p q : ℕ) (K : Type*) [Field K] [NumberField K]
    (𝔭 : IsDedekindDomain.HeightOneSpectrum (NumberField.RingOfIntegers K))
    (K' : Type*) [Field K'] [Algebra (𝔭.adicCompletion K) K']
    [IsSepClosure (𝔭.adicCompletion K) K'] : Prop :=
  (∃ x : Gal(K'/𝔭.adicCompletion K),
      NK.LocalAnabelian.IsFrobeniusFor (κ := 𝔭.adicCompletion K) (K' := K') p q x ∧
        NK.LocalTame.IsTameFrobeniusLift q
          (NK.LocalTame.wildInertiaSubgroup (κ := 𝔭.adicCompletion K) (K' := K') p)
          (NK.LocalAnabelian.inertiaSubgroup (κ := 𝔭.adicCompletion K) (K' := K') p) x) ∧
    (∀ x : Gal(K'/𝔭.adicCompletion K),
      NK.LocalTame.IsTameFrobeniusLift q
        (NK.LocalTame.wildInertiaSubgroup (κ := 𝔭.adicCompletion K) (K' := K') p)
        (NK.LocalAnabelian.inertiaSubgroup (κ := 𝔭.adicCompletion K) (K' := K') p) x →
      NK.LocalAnabelian.ActsAsFrobenius (κ := 𝔭.adicCompletion K) (K' := K') p q x)

/-- **The abelianised tame quotient** (Shimizu, arXiv:2009.10431, Lemma 2.1).

For `κ = K_𝔭` a `p`-adic field with residue field of `q` elements,

  `G_κ^{tr,ab} = (G_κ/V_κ)^{ab} ≅ Ẑ × μ_{q-1}`.

Classically, local reciprocity identifies `G_κ^{ab}` with `κˣ^{∧}`, the structure theory of the
units gives `κˣ ≅ ℤ × μ_{q-1} × U¹` with `U¹ = 1 + 𝔪_κ` pro-`p`, and killing the image of the
wild inertia (a pro-`p` group, mapping onto the pro-`p` part `(U¹)^{∧}`) leaves `Ẑ × μ_{q-1}`. -/
def TameAbelianisationStructure (p q : ℕ) (K : Type*) [Field K] [NumberField K]
    (𝔭 : IsDedekindDomain.HeightOneSpectrum (NumberField.RingOfIntegers K))
    (K' : Type*) [Field K'] [Algebra (𝔭.adicCompletion K) K']
    [IsSepClosure (𝔭.adicCompletion K) K'] : Prop :=
  Nonempty (NK.LocalTame.tameAbelianization (κ := 𝔭.adicCompletion K) (K' := K') p ≃*
    (NK.LocalAnabelian.Zhat × Multiplicative (ZMod (q - 1))))

/-- **The structure of the unit group of a `p`-adic field** (local class field theory side:
Serre, *Local Fields*, Ch. II §5).  `κˣ ≅ ℤ × μ_{q-1} × U¹` with `U¹ = 1 + 𝔪_κ` a pro-`p` group;
equivalently, the profinite completion `κˣ^{∧}` of the unit group has a *pro-`p`* normal subgroup
`U` (the image of `U¹`) with `κˣ^{∧} ⧸ U ≅ Ẑ × μ_{q-1}`.

This is the single statement about `κˣ` to which the abelianisation component of the local
structure theorem reduces; see `NK.TameStructure.TameAbelianisationViaUnits`. -/
def UnitsStructure (p q : ℕ) (κ : Type*) [Field κ] : Prop :=
  ∃ U : Subgroup (NK.LocalReciprocity.completionUnits κ), U.Normal ∧
    NK.LocalTame.IsProP p ↥U ∧
    Nonempty ((NK.LocalReciprocity.completionUnits κ) ⧸ U ≃*
      (NK.LocalAnabelian.Zhat × Multiplicative (ZMod (q - 1))))

/-- **Shimizu, arXiv:2009.10431, Lemma 2.1, in `κˣ`-form** — the reduction of the abelianised tame
quotient to the units.

Local reciprocity gives `κˣ^{∧} ≅ G_κ^{ab}` (`NK.LocalCFT.Completion.exists_mulEquiv_unitsCompletion`)
and the wild inertia `V_κ` — a pro-`p` group — maps onto the pro-`p` part `U` of `κˣ^{∧}`; hence

  `G_κ^{tr,ab} = G_κ^{ab}/V_κ ≅ κˣ^{∧} ⧸ U`,

and by the structure of the units `U` may be taken pro-`p`.  The two `Nonempty`s below record
these two identifications for a *common* `U`: the first is the class-field-theoretic statement
that the abelianised tame quotient is the quotient of `κˣ^{∧}` by the image of the wild inertia,
the second is the structure of the units (`NK.TameStructure.UnitsStructure`, Serre II §5). -/
def TameAbelianisationViaUnits (p q : ℕ) (κ K' : Type*) [Field κ] [Field K'] [Algebra κ K']
    [IsSepClosure κ K'] : Prop :=
  ∃ U : Subgroup (NK.LocalReciprocity.completionUnits κ), U.Normal ∧
    NK.LocalTame.IsProP p ↥U ∧
    Nonempty (NK.LocalTame.tameAbelianization (κ := κ) (K' := K') p ≃*
      (NK.LocalReciprocity.completionUnits κ ⧸ U)) ∧
    Nonempty ((NK.LocalReciprocity.completionUnits κ) ⧸ U ≃*
      (NK.LocalAnabelian.Zhat × Multiplicative (ZMod (q - 1))))

/-- The bundle of the named classical inputs: everything the assembly of
`NK.TameData.TameDataInput p (residueCard K 𝔭) (K_𝔭) K'` needs. -/
structure TameStructureInputs (p q : ℕ) (K : Type*) [Field K] [NumberField K]
    (𝔭 : IsDedekindDomain.HeightOneSpectrum (NumberField.RingOfIntegers K))
    (K' : Type*) [Field K'] [Algebra (𝔭.adicCompletion K) K']
    [IsSepClosure (𝔭.adicCompletion K) K'] : Prop where
  /-- the residue characteristic is `p`: `CharP (ResidueField 𝒪_κ) p` -/
  charP : CharP (IsLocalRing.ResidueField (𝔭.adicCompletionIntegers K)) p
  /-- NSW (7.5.6): `Gal(κ^ur/κ) ≅ Ẑ` -/
  unramified : UnramifiedZhat p K 𝔭 K'
  /-- NSW (7.5.7) Corollary, (7.5.11): the structure of the tame inertia -/
  tameInertia : TameInertiaStructure p K 𝔭 K'
  /-- NSW (12.1.8), Iwasawa: the Frobenius normalisation -/
  frobenius : FrobeniusNormalisation p q K 𝔭 K'
  /-- Shimizu 2.1, via local class field theory: `G_κ^{tr,ab} ≅ Ẑ × μ_{q-1}` -/
  abelianisation : TameAbelianisationStructure p q K 𝔭 K'

end

end NK.TameStructure
